    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωκ-άομαι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶκος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mimic</i>, and so,
				<i>ridicule</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				1.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.27
			</span></i>: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωκώμενος</span>
			<i>in jest</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεποιθώς</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3p.62U.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.38
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μωκωμένη διάλεκτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agatharch.
					21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσφορὰ μεμωκημένη</span>
				(v.l.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεμωμ</span>-) offering <i>made in
			mockery</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Si.</u>
				31
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				34
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Je.</u>
				28(51).18
			</span></i>.—
				Act.
			 only in <i><span class="en">
				Cyr.
			</span></i> (Said to be formed from the sound made by a camel, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάμηλος μωκᾶται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			
			<i>de</i>
			
			<i>voc.animal.</i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stud.Ital.</u>
				1.93
			</span></i>; =
			<i>mugio,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>)</div>
